course: dictionary
lesson: 6382
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «A mule is strong and sure-footed, but it almost never has young of its own.» The clues are strong, sure-footed and young, so mule here is an animal.
explain: The same word can describe a person. «He is as stubborn as a mule and will not change his mind.» Stubborn is the clue. A mule is a person who will not budge, so this is the informal meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Ask: does this still make sense? If you read «a slipper with no back» in place of mule, the sentence still works, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A word with several meanings is called a word with more than one sense.
fact: A mule is an animal whose mother is a horse and whose father is a donkey.
fact: «Stubborn as a mule» is an informal phrase for someone who will not change their mind.
fact: A mule can also be a slipper or shoe with no back.
fact: In slang, a mule is a person who carries illegal drugs or money across borders for criminals.
exercise: «A mule is strong and used for carrying loads.» What is a mule in this sentence? | *An animal whose mother is a horse and father is a donkey | A very stubborn person | A person who carries illegal goods | A slipper with no back
exercise: Grandad says his cousin is «stubborn as a mule». What does this mean? | Strong and good at carrying loads | Quick and sure on his feet | Lost on a mountain path | *Very stubborn, and will not change his mind
exercise: «Ella put on her old mules before breakfast.» Which meaning fits best? | A person who carries illegal goods | An animal used for carrying loads | *A slipper or shoe with no back | A stubborn person
test: «Mules almost never have babies of their own.» What does this show about mules in science? | A mule can only be a slipper | A mule is a stubborn person | A mule is a kind of horse | *A mule is a hybrid, a cross between two kinds of animal
test: «The police warned that a mule had carried money across the border for the gang.» Which meaning of mule is used? | A very stubborn person | A slipper with no back | *A person who carries illegal money or drugs across borders for criminals | An animal used for carrying loads
exam: «The mule track wound up the mountain, and each mule carried heavy sacks of salt.» Which meaning of mule is used here? | A stubborn person | A person who carries illegal goods | *An animal used for carrying loads | A slipper with no back
